        "problem": "An eagle flies along the parametric curve\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{t}{5}),\\,y=y(t),\\,t>0,\n$$\n\nwhere $x$ and $y$ are measured in meters relative to its nest at the origin, and $t$ is measured in seconds. The functions ${x}^{′}(t)$ and ${y}^{′}(t)$ give the eagle's horizontal and vertical velocity, respectively.",
