  "live_records": {
    "q-133285": {
      "dom_id": "question-133285",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Calculate the horizontal velocity of the eagle as a function of time.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The horizontal velocity of the bird is$\\,$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $\\,\\text{m/s}.$",
      "worked_solution": "The horizontal velocity of the eagle is given by ${x}^{′}(t),$ where \n\n$$\nx(t)=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{t}{5}).\n$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of arctangent is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡t)=\\frac{1}{1+{t}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{t}{5})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+(t/5)^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{t}{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+{t}^{2}/25}\\cdot \\frac{1}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{25+{t}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the horizontal velocity of the eagle is given by the function ${x}^{′}(t)=\\frac{5}{25+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{m/s}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
